Q: PHP Variable Naming A: <p>You can use <code>$$</code><br />
That way, you can use a variable named by a variable name.</p>
<p>From your example, it would be:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php

$_tbl = 2;

$varFldType = &quot;tbl{$_tbl}Fld_type&quot;;
$tbl_Fld_type = $$varFldType;

$varFormTypes = &quot;tbl{$_tbl}FormTypes&quot;;
$tbl_FormTypes = $$varFormTypes;
</code></pre>
<p>That is actually answering what you just asked.</p>
